hamlet has been having delusions  hallucinations anhedonia lack of  motivation and poor speech he sees  ghosts and all denmark thinks he's crazy  but what is actually happening you  being the smarty pants that you are  diagnosed him with schizophrenia  most people believe that schizophrenia  is caused by abnormal dopamine activity  in the brain  dopamine is a neurotransmitter that is  expressed in the central nervous system  and regulates things like motivation  cognition emotions and the reward system  dopamine binds to dopamine receptors  which are g-protein-coupled receptors  that are located in the postsynaptic  membrane this changes the structure of  the receptor which can then activate a  nearby g protein by exchanging the  bounded gdp molecule for a gtp molecule  once activated the g protein splits with  its alpha subunit and the bound gtp  moving to bind to adenylyl cyclase  the adenylyl cyclase is then activated  producing cyclic amp  and spreading the signal throughout the  cell schizophrenic patients have a  neural activity at dopamine receptors  specifically d2 receptors with increased  dopamine levels in the mesolimbic area  of the brain  and decreased levels in the prefrontal  cortex increased levels cause positive  symptoms like hallucinations and  delusions while decreased levels cause  negative and cognitive symptoms  like lack of motivation and decreased  levels of emotional expression because  of the true cause of schizophrenia is  unclear treatment aims to reduce  symptoms instead  antipsychotic drugs specifically  risperidone binds to neurotransmitters  like the d2 receptor  and inhibits dopamine from binding which  alleviates positive negative and  cognitive symptoms  however treatment doesn't always work  some are unresponsive to medication  most drugs only reduce positive symptoms  not negative or cognitive ones  and antipsychotics have severe side  effects and in general schizophrenia  prevents people from leading normal  lives  they can't form relationships or get an  education or job and need constant  support to manage symptoms  therefore social awareness is needed to  help those with schizophrenia  understanding schizophrenia can support  patients especially ones with suicidal  or unhealthy lives  decrease re-hospitalization and  stigmatization monitor treatments and  bring them closer to normal life  and there we go how can you help hamlet  and others like him  you
 

